GOAL : Make a better stocksim (make it both visual and make the code more efficient)
Learn: some database method

1. Import a free finance API (yfinance) and create a function to gte the price, it will try to get the fastest, most recent price based on the ticker symbol, if it cant find the price then it will look at the history to get the price and if both methods dont work then in tehory the ticker is not real therfore it returns it as an error / 0.
2. TickerTracker Class, I need a class to find out everything i need to display when it comes to the ticker. To get the methods you need to enter a ticker, the amount, and the avg price which i will get later with the yfinace function. Errors are returned if an input is incorrect. get_entire_cost method: amount x price. update current price method: takes the new current price and changes the current price into it. profit n loss and percentage: (made to be displayed visually later), takes current market price - price they bought * by the amount they bought and made into a percentage in the other method. repr was used to test it.
3. User Class, The most important class which allows this project to actually function. Allows for a input of a name, and start money (defaults at 10k). Also gave it a inv dictionary attribute to store what the user owns. BUY Method: requires input of ticker, amount bought and the value of each ticker. If the user has less money than required then a value error is raised, otherwise then the user's money is updated. If the ticker is not inside of the dictionary then it creates a ticker object and puts the ticker as the key for it. Otherwise if the ticker is already in the invintory of the user it will get the ticker object(value of tracked inv ticker) and it will calculate the new cost by adding the bought value to the value thats already there and same with the amount. Then it will update the attributes of the object thats linked to the tracked inv ticker. SELL method: requires the same input as the buying method. 3 options. 1: not in inv = raises a value error. 2: Inside of the inv but not enough to be sold = raises a value error, 3. Can be sold = the user's money increases and the amount in the inv of that specific ticker decreases based on it. And if the amount of the ticker reaches 0 the ticker is deleted from the inv.
